  "enisaUuid": "e177cdd7-e0eb-35be-b98b-a11cdfd8d9cd",
  "description": "A vulnerability was identified in Backdrop CMS up to 1.35.2. Affected is the function get_argument of the file core/modules/views/plugins/views_plugin_argument_default_php.inc of the component Views Module. Such manipulation leads to incorrect authorization. The attack can be launched remotely. The exploit is publicly available and might be used. The config-import path enforces no 'use PHP for settings' check while the Views PHP-code argument plugin executes eval() without a permission check, confirming the authorization bypass. The vendor explains: \"As per our security advisory policy, no security advisory is required when an exploit requires 'advanced permissions'.\"",
